# RepoLens AI Development Rules

## Project Goal

You are helping build RepoLens AI — a production-inspired AI-powered Code Documentation Assistant (take-home assignment).

Optimize for **readability and maintainability**, not complexity. Demonstrate excellent engineering practices with a clean, scalable application.

## Approved Tech Stack

Do not introduce additional technologies unless explicitly requested.

| Layer | Technologies |
|-------|-------------|
| Framework | Next.js App Router, React, TypeScript |
| Styling | Tailwind CSS, shadcn/ui |
| AI | OpenAI, GPT-4o-mini, text-embedding-3-small |
| Vector DB | Qdrant |
| Metadata DB | SQLite, Drizzle ORM |
| Parsing | Tree-sitter |
| Validation | Zod |
| Testing | Vitest |

## Architecture

Follow this dependency flow — never violate it:

```
UI → API Routes → Services → Repositories → Database / External Clients
```

- Business logic must **never** exist inside Route Handlers.
- API Routes should only: validate requests, call services, return responses.

## Folder Responsibilities

| Directory | Purpose |
|-----------|---------|
| `app/` | Pages, layouts, API routes only — no business logic |
| `components/` | Reusable UI components |
| `features/` | Feature-specific UI |
| `server/services/` | Business logic |
| `server/repositories/` | SQLite access only |
| `server/clients/` | External services (OpenAI, Qdrant) |
| `lib/` | Pure helper utilities |
| `config/` | Application configuration |
| `types/` | Shared TypeScript types |

## TypeScript

- Strict typing always; never use `any`.
- Prefer explicit return types.
- Interfaces for shared models; type aliases for unions.

## Code Style

Small functions, single responsibility, readable naming. Avoid nested conditionals. Extract reusable helpers; avoid duplicated logic.

## Validation

Every API request must be validated with Zod. Never trust client input.

## Error Handling

Never swallow errors. Return meaningful error responses. Log unexpected exceptions.

## UI

- shadcn/ui + Tailwind CSS only — no inline styles.
- Every page: loading state, empty state, error state.
- Dark mode compatible.

## Performance

Batch embedding requests. Stream AI responses. Avoid loading entire repositories into memory. Reuse existing utilities.

## Security

- Validate uploaded ZIP files; prevent Zip Slip attacks.
- Ignore: `node_modules`, `.git`, `build`, `dist`.
- Reject unsupported file types.

## Comments

Only explain **why** — do not comment obvious code.

## AI Behaviour

Before generating implementation code:

1. Briefly explain the approach.
2. Mention any important trade-offs.

Never create unnecessary files. Do not over-engineer. Follow the agreed architecture. If an architectural decision is unclear, ask before changing it.
